# cp elasticsearch.env.example elasticsearch.env and fill it in. elasticsearch.env is gitignored.
#
# Password for the built-in `elastic` user. It is set on first boot and then lives in the
# cluster's own security index — changing this value later does *not* change the password on
# an existing volume, it just makes the article service stop authenticating. Rotate through
# the ES API, then update this.
ELASTIC_PASSWORD=
